{0 ocgio}

The {b ocgio} package provides OCaml bindings for GIO: I/O, files, and the
application and networking abstractions from GLib's application framework.
They are generated from GIO's GObject introspection data.

{%html:<a href="../ocgtk/conventions.html">The conventions page</a>%} explains how the bindings are organised and how GObject maps onto OCaml.

{1 Modules}

The library is reached as {!Ocgio}, with one module per class, interface or
record, such as {!Ocgio.File} and {!Ocgio.Application}.

{b {{!page-modules}All classes, interfaces and records}}

{ul
{- {!Ocgio.Enums} — enumerations and bitfields. }
{- {!Ocgio.Constants} — constants. }
{- {!Ocgio.Raw} — the C externals and abstract types the modules above are
   built on. }
}

{1 Dependencies}

It builds on {!Ocglib} (GLib and GObject).
